// sf_channel.bsm — the mixer channels.
//
// sound_fusion has SF_NTRACKS channels. Each channel is a volume fader plus a
// fixed FOUR-slot insert chain: a moon_filter (the Moog ladder), then a
// zener_comp (the TG12345-style channel compressor), then a morricone_spring
// (the spring reverb), then a rotary (Leslie) — docs/plans/sound_fusion.md
// slice 5a/5b/8/9. Four concrete plugin kinds, in a fixed natural channel-strip
// order (shape the tone, tame the dynamics, add the room, then spin the stereo
// field — the same order a real console drives filter -> compressor -> reverb
// -> modulation), so this stays named slots rather than a generic N-deep
// polymorphic chain. The original two-slot comment here said "a third insert
// kind is the trigger to generalize" — the trigger fired, and the answer is
// still a concrete named slot, not a dynamic chain. Rule 20's bar is about HOW
// MANY CONSUMERS justify promoting something to a shared, reusable place (each
// insert's DSP graduated INTO an stb cartridge — stbfilter / stbdynamics /
// stbreverb — wrapped as a standalone tools/ plugin, the same two-layer shape)
// — it does not mandate a generic dispatch mechanism for a fixed, known signal
// chain. The FOURTH kind (the spring reverb) has since arrived and kept the
// named-slot model exactly: it has a natural fixed position (a mono insert
// after the compressor, before the pan — a spring tank is a mono device, so
// stereo width belongs to a later plate/hall, not here). Revisit only if a
// kind shows up with no natural fixed position.
// This module owns the channel array; the timeline and the tools reach a
// channel only through the functions here.

// One mixer channel: a volume, a pan position, and the three-slot insert
// chain (moon_filter, then compressor, then rotary — all three allocated
// once at init, each independently engaged via its own `_on` flag). `pan`
// is the constant-power pan position in [-1, 1] (-1 hard left, 0 centre,
// +1 hard right). `stereo` is the source-shape flag (0 = mono source,
// panned into the field — the Moog-bass case; 1 = stereo source, L/R
// processed separately) — see sf_channel_process. `gain_l`/`gain_r` are
// the precomputed constant-power pan gains (cos/sin of the pan angle) so
// the per-frame strip multiplies by a stored constant instead of calling
// cos/sin every sample — pan is constant per track, so the trig belongs at
// set-time, not in the hot loop. New fields are appended so the typed
// accessors below keep their offsets.
// The trailing six fields CACHE each insert's user-facing parameters on the
// channel itself (cutoff/reso/slope for the Moog, mode/release for the
// compressor, mode for the rotary). The plugin instances hold their own
// coefficients but expose no getter, so the channel keeps the source-of-truth
// values the GUI reads back to draw a slider and writes when the user drags it
// — the same "cache the value at set-time" shape gain_l/gain_r already use.
// `comp_thr` caches the compressor threshold in dB (the practical "drive into
// the compressor" control — without it the default -6 dBFS leaves the comp
// nearly silent on a typical signal). `muted`/`solo` are the mixer's per-channel
// flags, read by sf_render's mix loop: a muted channel is skipped, and when ANY
// channel is soloed only soloed channels play.
struct Track { vol: float, flt_on, flt, pan: float, stereo, gain_l: float, gain_r: float, rot_on, rot, comp_on, comp, cutoff: float, reso: float, slope, comp_mode, comp_rel, rot_mode, comp_thr: float, muted, solo, spring_on, spring, spring_decay: float, spring_damp: float, spring_mix: float }

static auto _sf_tracks;     // malloc(SF_NTRACKS * sizeof(Track))

// Set a channel's pan position and precompute its constant-power gains ONCE.
// theta in [0, pi/2] (centre = pi/4 → gain_l = gain_r = 0.707, equal power).
// Called at init and from sf_track_set — never per frame.
static void _sf_apply_pan(tk: Track, pan: float) {
    auto theta: float;
    tk.pan    = pan;
    theta     = (pan + 1.0) * 0.78539816;     // (pan + 1) * pi/4
    tk.gain_l = cos_f(theta);
    tk.gain_r = sin_f(theta);
}

// Allocate the channels and give each a sensible default: 80% volume, all
// four insert slots off, and a fresh moon_filter + compressor + spring +
// rotary instance each. Call once at engine init.
void sf_channel_init() {
    auto tr, tk: Track;
    _sf_tracks = malloc(SF_NTRACKS * sizeof(Track));
    for (tr = 0; tr < SF_NTRACKS; tr++) {
        tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
        tk.vol    = 0.8;
        tk.flt_on = 0;
        tk.flt    = moon_new(44100.0);
        tk.comp_on = 0;
        tk.comp    = zener_new(44100.0);
        tk.rot_on = 0;
        tk.rot    = rotary_new(44100.0);
        tk.spring_on = 0;
        tk.spring    = morricone_new(44100.0);
        tk.stereo = 0;     // mono source (panned into the stereo field)
        // Cached insert parameters with musical defaults, applied the first
        // time the user engages each insert from the GUI. These never touch
        // the render until the matching `_on` flag is set, so the all-inserts-
        // off baseline stays byte-identical.
        // The mode/release values are written as their literal enum values
        // (named in the comment) because the defining cartridges expose them as
        // plain `const`, which does not reach a `load`ed module like this one
        // — the same cross-module rule sf_lib.bsm documents for SF_NTRACKS.
        tk.cutoff    = 1200.0;   // Moog corner, Hz
        tk.reso      = 0.3;      // gentle resonance
        tk.slope     = 4;        // -24 dB/oct (full 4-pole ladder)
        tk.comp_mode = 0;        // COMP_COMPRESS (2:1, the gentle mode)
        tk.comp_rel  = 1;        // COMP_REL_250 (250 ms release)
        tk.rot_mode  = 1;        // ROTARY_CHORALE (slow rotation when engaged)
        // -18 dBFS so engaging the compressor on a typical channel signal
        // (~-6 dBFS here) produces audible gain reduction immediately, rather
        // than the near-silent default the stbdynamics -6 dB threshold gives.
        tk.comp_thr  = 0.0 - 18.0;
        // Spring reverb (Morricone) defaults: a medium tail, lightly damped,
        // a subtle send — inert until spring_on is set from the GUI.
        tk.spring_decay = 0.84;
        tk.spring_damp  = 0.2;
        tk.spring_mix   = 0.3;
        tk.muted     = 0;
        tk.solo      = 0;
        _sf_apply_pan(tk, 0.0);   // centre
    }
}

// Configure one channel's volume and filter insert. `slope` selects the ladder
// tap (1..4 poles = -6..-24 dB/oct). The plugin computes its coefficients here
// so the render loop only has to process samples.
void sf_track_set(tr, vol: float, flt_on, cutoff: float, reso: float, slope, pan: float) {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    tk.vol    = vol;
    _sf_apply_pan(tk, pan);
    tk.flt_on = flt_on;
    tk.cutoff = cutoff;
    tk.reso   = reso;
    tk.slope  = slope;
    if (flt_on != 0) { moon_set(tk.flt, cutoff, reso, slope); }
}

// Configure ONLY the filter insert (engage/bypass + cutoff/reso/slope),
// leaving volume and pan untouched — the GUI's per-channel filter controls
// want to change just the filter without re-supplying vol/pan, the same focused
// shape sf_track_set_volume / sf_track_set_compressor / sf_track_set_rotary
// already follow. The cached cutoff/reso/slope keep the GUI's slider readout in
// sync with what the plugin is actually running.
void sf_track_set_filter(tr, flt_on, cutoff: float, reso: float, slope) {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    tk.flt_on = flt_on;
    tk.cutoff = cutoff;
    tk.reso   = reso;
    tk.slope  = slope;
    if (flt_on != 0) { moon_set(tk.flt, cutoff, reso, slope); }
}

// Set just one channel's volume, leaving the insert/pan untouched — the
// GUI's interactive faders (lane header bar + mixer strip) want to change
// ONLY volume on every drag frame, and routing that through sf_track_set
// would force the caller to also re-supply flt_on/cutoff/reso/slope/pan
// (which the GUI doesn't cache) just to avoid silently resetting them.
void sf_track_set_volume(tr, vol: float) {
    auto tk: Track;
    if (vol < 0.0) { vol = 0.0; }
    if (vol > 1.0) { vol = 1.0; }
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    tk.vol = vol;
}

// Configure one channel's compressor insert. `mode` is COMP_COMPRESS (2:1)
// or COMP_LIMIT (8:1); `release_idx` is one of the six fixed steps
// (COMP_REL_100 .. COMP_REL_5000, zener_comp.bsm) — the same "few
// switches, each definitive" surface the TG12345's own dynamics section
// had. Attack is NOT exposed here either, for the same reason
// zener_comp.bsm doesn't expose a setter for it: it's fixed at 8ms.
// A separate setter from sf_track_set for the same reason the rotary gets
// one — a logically independent concern, kept out of the kitchen-sink
// parameter list.
void sf_track_set_compressor(tr, comp_on, mode, release_idx) {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    tk.comp_on   = comp_on;
    tk.comp_mode = mode;
    tk.comp_rel  = release_idx;
    if (comp_on != 0) {
        zener_set_mode(tk.comp, mode);
        zener_set_release(tk.comp, release_idx);
        zener_set_threshold_db(tk.comp, tk.comp_thr);   // apply the cached threshold
    }
}

// Set ONLY the compressor threshold in dB — the GUI's threshold slider drags
// this every frame without re-supplying mode/release. Applied to the live
// plugin only while the insert is engaged, the same on-flag guard the mode/
// release setter uses.
void sf_track_set_comp_threshold(tr, threshold_db: float) {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    tk.comp_thr = threshold_db;
    if (tk.comp_on != 0) { zener_set_threshold_db(tk.comp, threshold_db); }
}

// Mute / solo a channel — written by the mixer's M/S buttons, read by
// sf_render's mix loop (a muted channel is skipped; any soloed channel makes
// every non-soloed channel silent). Pure flags here; the render owns the policy.
void sf_track_set_mute(tr, m) {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    tk.muted = m;
}
void sf_track_set_solo(tr, s) {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    tk.solo = s;
}

// Set ONLY the pan position [-1, 1], recomputing the constant-power gains —
// the GUI's pan control writes this without disturbing volume or the inserts,
// the focused-setter shape sf_track_set_volume already follows.
void sf_track_set_pan(tr, pan: float) {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    _sf_apply_pan(tk, pan);
}

// Configure one channel's rotary insert. `mode` is ROTARY_OFF /
// ROTARY_CHORALE / ROTARY_TREMOLO (stbrotary.bsm). A separate setter from
// sf_track_set because the rotary is a logically independent concern (and
// keeps sf_track_set's own parameter list from growing further) — same
// shape as moon_filter's own cutoff/reso/slope group.
void sf_track_set_rotary(tr, rot_on, mode) {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    tk.rot_on   = rot_on;
    tk.rot_mode = mode;
    if (rot_on != 0) { rotary_set_mode(tk.rot, mode); }
}

// Configure one channel's spring-reverb insert. `decay` is the tail length
// (0..<1), `damping` the tone of the tail (0 = bright, 1 = dark), `mix` the
// dry/wet blend (0..1). Applied to the live plugin only while engaged, the same
// on-flag guard the other inserts use. A focused setter so each of the GUI's
// three drag-bars can re-supply the group (reading the other two back) without
// disturbing the other inserts — the same shape sf_track_set_filter follows.
void sf_track_set_spring(tr, spring_on, decay: float, damping: float, mix: float) {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    tk.spring_on    = spring_on;
    tk.spring_decay = decay;
    tk.spring_damp  = damping;
    tk.spring_mix   = mix;
    if (spring_on != 0) { morricone_set(tk.spring, decay, damping, mix); }
}

// Clear every channel's insert state. The render calls this before a pass so
// neither insert carries memory across renders.
void sf_channel_reset_filters() {
    auto tr, tk: Track;
    for (tr = 0; tr < SF_NTRACKS; tr++) {
        tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
        moon_reset(tk.flt);
        zener_reset(tk.comp);
        morricone_reset(tk.spring);
        rotary_reset(tk.rot);
    }
}

// Read accessors for the GUI (which must not touch the private channel array).
sf_channel_vol(tr) -> float {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    return tk.vol;
}
sf_channel_flt_on(tr) {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    return tk.flt_on;
}
sf_channel_comp_on(tr) {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    return tk.comp_on;
}
sf_channel_rot_on(tr) {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    return tk.rot_on;
}

// Insert parameter read accessors — the GUI draws each insert's current
// setting (slider position, mode label) from these and writes a changed value
// back through the matching setter above. Reading the cached value rather than
// the plugin's internal coefficients keeps the GUI on the channel's public
// surface, never reaching into a plugin instance.
sf_channel_flt_cutoff(tr) -> float {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    return tk.cutoff;
}
sf_channel_flt_reso(tr) -> float {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    return tk.reso;
}
sf_channel_flt_slope(tr) {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    return tk.slope;
}
sf_channel_comp_mode(tr) {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    return tk.comp_mode;
}
sf_channel_comp_rel(tr) {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    return tk.comp_rel;
}
sf_channel_rot_mode(tr) {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    return tk.rot_mode;
}
sf_channel_comp_thr(tr) -> float {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    return tk.comp_thr;
}
sf_channel_muted(tr) {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    return tk.muted;
}
sf_channel_solo(tr) {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    return tk.solo;
}
sf_channel_pan(tr) -> float {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    return tk.pan;
}
sf_channel_spring_on(tr) {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    return tk.spring_on;
}
sf_channel_spring_decay(tr) -> float {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    return tk.spring_decay;
}
sf_channel_spring_damp(tr) -> float {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    return tk.spring_damp;
}
sf_channel_spring_mix(tr) -> float {
    auto tk: Track;
    tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    return tk.spring_mix;
}

// 1 if ANY channel is soloed — the render asks this once per pass to decide
// whether solo gating is in effect (when nothing is soloed, every unmuted
// channel plays normally).
sf_any_solo() {
    auto tr, tk: Track;
    for (tr = 0; tr < SF_NTRACKS; tr++) {
        tk = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
        if (tk.solo != 0) { return 1; }
    }
    return 0;
}

// Run one dry sample through channel `tr` and return its STEREO (L, R)
// contribution — the per-channel strip the mix loop calls every frame. This is
// the headline multi-return consumer: two floats home in d0/d1, no struct, no
// memory (a C++ `std::pair`/out-param would cost more).
//
// Mono source (tk.stereo == 0 — the common case, e.g. a Moog bass): the Moog
// insert runs ONCE, then the compressor (when engaged) tames the dynamics, then
// the spring reverb (when engaged) adds the room — all three in the MONO stage,
// BEFORE the fader — gain-staging order: shape the tone, control the level, add
// the space, then trim with the fader, the same order the TG12345's own channel
// strip used. The wet, post-fader sample is placed into the field by a
// constant-power pan (equal power left+right, -3 dB at centre). The
// rotary — when engaged — runs AFTER pan, on the now-stereo (L, R) pair, the
// same position it occupies in stbmixer's master stage (a rotary modulates a
// stereo signal; it has nothing to do before there's a stereo signal to
// modulate). A stereo-source track would run the Moog insert twice
// (independent L/R state) — same (float,float) return, the flag only gates
// the pass count — and lands with stereo clip import (S2); until a stereo
// source exists, building that branch would be speculative.
sf_channel_process(tr, dry: float) -> (float, float) {
    auto tk: Track, wet: float, l: float, r: float;
    tk  = _sf_tracks + tr * sizeof(Track);
    wet = dry;
    if (tk.flt_on != 0) { wet = moon_process(tk.flt, wet); }
    if (tk.comp_on != 0) { wet = zener_process(tk.comp, wet); }
    // Spring reverb sits in the MONO stage (before the pan): a real spring tank
    // is a mono device, so the wet is panned into the field together with the
    // dry, like an amp in a fixed position. Stereo width is a later plate/hall's job.
    if (tk.spring_on != 0) { wet = morricone_process(tk.spring, wet); }
    wet *= tk.vol;
    // Constant-power pan via the precomputed per-track gains (no trig in the
    // hot loop — see _sf_apply_pan).
    l = wet * tk.gain_l;
    r = wet * tk.gain_r;
    if (tk.rot_on != 0) { l, r = rotary_tick(tk.rot, l, r); }
    return l, r;
}
